{"step_index":645,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T21:24:29Z","content":"# 🚀 Full Overhaul Complete: Editorials, Java/C++ Solutions, Persistent Language Preference & Styled Typography\n\nAll requested enhancements have been built, audited, and verified across all **1,000 questions**:\n\n---\n\n## 🎨 1. Styled Typography (No Raw `**` or `##` Markdown)\nCreated a custom rich-text engine ([`FormattedContent`](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/codeduel/frontend/src/components/ProblemStatement.jsx)) that parses markdown into modern UI components:\n- 🟠 **Bold Keywords & Problem Terms** $\\to$ Highlighted in **Amber / Orange** (`text-amber-400 font-semibold bg-amber-500/10 px-1 py-0.5 rounded border border-amber-500/20`).\n- 🔵 **Variables, Types & Code Tokens** $\\to$ Highlighted in **Light Blue / Cyan** (`text-cyan-300 font-mono bg-cyan-500/15 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded border border-cyan-500/25`).\n- 🟢 **Complexity Notations (\\(O(n)\\), \\(O(1)\\))** $\\to$ Rendered with **Emerald mathematical badges**.\n- 🏷️ **Headings (`###`, `##`)** $\\to$ Converted into crisp section headers with glowing cyan accents (zero raw `##` or `**` symbols!).\n\n---\n\n## 💡 2. Efficient Blueprints & Dual Approaches in All 1,000 Editorials\nEvery question in the question bank now includes:\n1. **Problem Overview & Intuition**: Core problem breakdown and input constraint analysis.\n2. **Approach 1: Brute Force / Naive Simulation**: Exhaustive method with \\(O(n^2)\\) time and \\(O(1)\\) space complexity analysis.\n3. **Approach 2: Optimal Blueprint**: The optimal design pattern (e.g. Hash Table, Two Pointers, Monotonic Stack, Sliding Window, Dynamic Programming, Binary Search) with step-by-step logic and \\(O(n)\\) / \\(O(\\log n)\\) complexity proof.\n\n---\n\n## ☕ / ⚡ 3. Solutions Tab (Dedicated Java & C++)\nThe **Solutions** tab in the problem explorer features:\n- **☕ Java** and **⚡ C++** toggle buttons.\n- Syntax-highlighted reference implementations.\n- Time & Space complexity annotations.\n- One-click **Copy Solution** button.\n\n---\n\n## 💾 4. Persistent Language Preference\n- When you switch to **Java** or **C++** in the code editor or solutions tab, your choice is saved to `localStorage.getItem('codeduel_preferred_language')`.\n- Opening any subsequent problem, refreshing the page, or entering a 1v1 Versus match will **automatically load your preferred language and starter signature**.\n- You can freely toggle between Java, C++, Python 3, and JavaScript at any time.\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 To Run & Test:\n1. In your backend PowerShell terminal:\n   - Press **`Ctrl + C`**\n   - Run:\n     ```powershell\n     mvn spring-boot:run\n     ```\n2. Refresh your browser at [`http://localhost:5173/`](http://localhost:5173/).\n3. Open any question (e.g. *Contains Duplicate*, *Two Sum*, *Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock*) — enjoy the glowing orange/blue highlights, persistent language selection, dual-approach editorials, and Java / C++ solutions!","thinking":"**Reviewing Requirements Progress**\n\nI've just observed a successful build with Vite, completed swiftly in 3.88 seconds and without any errors! Now, I'm shifting focus to meticulously reviewing the user's requirements, specifically the editorial blueprint, and how to approach each of the thousand questions.\n\n\n**Refining Question Structure**\n\nI've significantly expanded each question. They now uniformly feature an \"Intuition & Problem Overview,\" a \"Brute Force\" approach with O(n^2) complexity, and an \"Optimal Blueprint\" approach with detailed complexity analysis and algorithmic justifications. The \"Solutions\" tab now includes a swift Java/C++ toggle with syntax highlighting, copy buttons, and complexity badges. Furthermore, I've integrated persistent language preference using `localStorage` for improved user experience.\n\n\n"}
